<title>SOUTH KOREA: Dong Ah plans $100 mln convertible issue.</title>
<headline>Dong Ah plans $100 mln convertible issue.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Dong Ah Construction Industrial Co said on Tuesday it had decided to issue $100 million worth of convertible bonds in Europe.  </p>
<p>A company statement said a detailed schedule would be announced later.</p>
<p>It said proceeds from the issue would be spent on the company's construction of the second phase of Libya's Great Man-made River project.</p>
<p>Dong Ah has been awarded the contract by the Libyan government.</p>
<p>The statement gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
